; c16-modal-hand. Anchor: shot-0234 (Ch. 16, other statistics).
; Printed: no number; the claim is that one shape is the most frequent.
; Claim: the commonest hand, by count of doubles and of void pip suits, has
;   two doubles and one void suit.
; State: none; a uniformly random hand of seven from the 28.
; Exact: 213255/1184040 = 0.1801, the largest cell; the next is one double
;   and no void, 191548/1184040.
;
; GAP deal-view (see c16-four-of-a-suit). The query is the modal cell for
;   one known hand under no trump.
(query
  (roles (chair v) (domino a) (domino b) (context q))
  (out)
  (pattern
    (viewer v)
    (double a)
    (double b)
    (holds v a)
    (holds v b)
    (none (roles (domino c))
      (double c) (not (tile c a)) (not (tile c b)) (holds v c))
    (not (context q q*))
    (none (roles (domino d)) (in d q) (holds v d))
    (none (roles (context r))
      (not (context r q*))
      (not (context r q))
      (none (roles (domino e)) (in e r) (holds v e)))))
